\v 28 \w Then\w* \w cried\w* \w Jesus\w* \w in\w* the \w temple\w* as he \w taught\w*, \w saying\w*, \wj  \+w Ye\+w* \+w both\+w* \+w know\+w* \+w me\+w*, \+w and\+w* \+w ye know\+w* \+w whence\+w* \+w I am\+w*: \+w and\+w* \+w I am\+w* \+w not\+w* \+w come\+w* \+w of\+w* \+w myself\+w*, \+w but\+w* \+w he that sent\+w* \+w me\+w* \+w is\+w* \+w true\+w*, \+w whom\+w* \+w ye\+w* \+w know\+w* \+w not\+w*.\wj*  
\v 29 \wj  \+w But\+w* \+w I\+w* \+w know\+w* \+w him\+w*: \+w for\+w* \+w I am\+w* \+w from\+w* \+w him\+w*, \+w and he\+w* \+w hath sent\+w* \+w me\+w*.\wj*  
\v 30 \w Then\w* they \w sought\w* to \w take\w* \w him\w*: \w but\w* no \w man\w* \w laid\w* \w hands\w* \w on\w* \w him\w*, \w because\w* \w his\w* \w hour\w* \w was\w* not \w yet\w* \w come\w*.  
